meta {
  name: Get Master Data
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseURL}}/v1/house/:house/young-persons/:youngPersonId/incidents/master-data
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  house: 4
  youngPersonId: 1
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}
docs {
  # Get Master Data

  This endpoint retrieves all master data/dropdown options for incidents.

  ## Response Structure:
  ```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "data": {
      "severity_levels": {
        "minor": "Minor",
        "moderate": "Moderate",
        "major": "Major",
        "critical": "Critical"
      },
      "incident_types": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "incident_type": "Physical Assault",
          "house_id": null,
          "client_id": null
        }
      ],
      "body_parts": [
        "No specific location",
        "Head",
        "Eye",
        "Nose"
      ],
      "yes_no": {
        "yes": "Yes",
        "no": "No"
      },
      "evidence_types": {
        "photo": "Photo",
        "video": "Video",
        "document": "Document",
        "audio": "Audio",
        "other": "Other"
      },
      "status": {
        "draft": "Draft",
        "pending_review": "Pending Review",
        "reviewed": "Reviewed",
        "closed": "Closed"
      }
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Master Data Fields:

  - **severity_levels** - Incident severity options (minor, moderate, major, critical)
  - **incident_types** - Collection of incident type records (global + house-specific)
  - **body_parts** - Body parts for injury reporting
  - **yes_no** - Yes/No options
  - **evidence_types** - Evidence file type categories (photo, video, document, audio, other)
  - **status** - Incident status options (draft, pending_review, reviewed, closed)

  ## Usage:
  Use this data to populate dropdowns and select fields in the incident form.
}